# actions.func

> Module: actions (İşlem Kayıtları) | Category: CORE

## Purpose
Audit log for all CRUD operations across the platform. Records every create, update, delete, and bulk delete action with user identity, timestamp, module, and data snapshot. Required for KVKK compliance.

**⚠️ STATUS: DEAD CODE** — ActionsPage.tsx is fully implemented (DataGrid, API calls, revert functionality) but has NO `<Route>` in App.tsx and NO sidebar entry. The component exists but cannot be reached by users.

## Problems It Solves
- KVKK (Turkish data protection law) requires audit trails
- Trace who made what change and when
- Revert accidental or malicious changes
- Compliance reporting for auditors

## Technical Database Structure
**Table:** `actions`
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | SERIAL PK | Unique identifier |
| tenant_id | INTEGER FK | Tenant isolation |
| kullanici_id | INTEGER FK | User who performed action |
| modul | VARCHAR(50) | Module name |
| eylem | action_type_enum | CREATE / UPDATE / DELETE / BULK_DELETE |
| kayit_id | INTEGER | Record ID affected |
| onceki_veri | JSONB | Data BEFORE change |
| sonraki_veri | JSONB | Data AFTER change |
| created_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | Timestamp |

**RLS:** Enabled (only shows actions for logged-in tenant)

## User Interface
**ActionsPage.tsx** — No route (dead code)
- DataGrid table: Modül, Eylem, Kayıt ID, Kullanıcı, Tarih
- Action type badges: green (create), blue (update), red (delete), orange (bulk delete)
- "Geri Al" (Revert) button per row for CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE
- Filter by module, action type, date
- Export to CSV/Excel/PDF

## API Endpoints
| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|:---:|-------------|
| GET | `/api/tenant/actions/` | Tenant JWT | List audit log (limit 200) |
| POST | `/api/tenant/actions/{id}/revert` | Tenant JWT | Revert action |

## Known Bugs
- **B-ACT-01 (P1):** ActionsPage component is unreachable — no `<Route>` and no sidebar entry. All code written but users cannot access it. Must add to App.tsx + Sidebar.tsx.

## Fix Required
```tsx
// In App.tsx:
<Route path="/dashboard/actions" element={<ActionsPage />} />

// In Sidebar.tsx navItems:
{ name: "İşlem Kayıtları", path: "/dashboard/actions", icon: History }
```

